Title: socket2: follow the native x86_64 ABIv1 socket ABI
Base: crates.io socket2 0.6.5 SHA-256 c3d1e2c7f27f8d4cb10542a02c49005dbd6e93095799d6f3be745fae9f8fedd4 plus PomAROS rust-aros 33325cbf1e271d2df213b65b2bcab0efc02b1a3d crate-store patch
Date: 2026-11-20
Status: local

ABIv1 has ip_mreq_source but not ip_mreqn. Do not select the
interface-index multicast API. The tagged socket adapter does not
implement sendmsg or recvmsg. Report Unsupported at those call sites.
Verification: SDK C and Rust ABI assertions, all-feature build, UDP
loopback payload and explicit message errors on x86_64 ABIv1.

--- a/src/sys/unix.rs
+++ b/src/sys/unix.rs
@@ -1165,6 +1165,12 @@
     msg: &mut MsgHdrMut<'_, '_, '_>,
     flags: c_int,
 ) -> io::Result<usize> {
+    #[cfg(all(target_os = "aros", target_abi = "abiv1"))]
+    {
+        let _ = (fd, msg, flags);
+        Err(io::ErrorKind::Unsupported.into())
+    }
+    #[cfg(not(all(target_os = "aros", target_abi = "abiv1")))]
     syscall!(recvmsg(fd, &mut msg.inner, flags)).map(|n| n as usize)
 }
 
